  <docidentifier type="ISO" primary="true">ISO 19107:2003</docidentifier>
  <docidentifier type="iso-reference">iso-reference ISO 19107:2003(E)</docidentifier>
  <docidentifier type="URN">URN urn:iso:std:iso:19107:stage-95.99</docidentifier><docidentifier scope="biblio-tag">ISO 19107:2003</docidentifier>
  <docnumber>19107</docnumber>
  <date type="published">
    <on>2003-05</on>
  </date>
  <contributor>
    <role type="publisher"/>
    <organization>
      
<name>International Organization for Standardization</name>

      <abbreviation>ISO</abbreviation>
      <uri>www.iso.org</uri>
    </organization>
  </contributor>
  <edition>1</edition>
  <language>en</language>
  <language>fr</language>
  <script>Latn</script>
  <abstract format="text/plain" language="en" script="Latn">ISO 19107:2003 specifies conceptual schemas for describing the spatial characteristics of geographic features, and a set of spatial operations consistent with these schemas. It treats vector geometry and topology up to three dimensions. It defines standard spatial operations for use in access, query, management, processing, and data exchange of geographic information for spatial (geometric and topological) objects of up to three topological dimensions embedded in coordinate spaces of up to three axes.</abstract>
  <status>
    <stage>95</stage>
    <substage>99</substage>
  </status>
